# protocol/01 § Joining: a private channel opened to 1,000 devices is populated by instance Add
# proposals in batches, at most 256 per commit, so the storm completes in four commits (256, 256,
# 256, 232). The instance keeps the batch - ProposeAddBatch queues it in pending_joins, proposes
# 256, and each accepted commit drains the next slice, re-checking every device's eligibility -
# and the Go harness asserts exactly four commits from the instance's own counter, one
# mls_welcome_payloads row per commit and an empty queue. Every joiner enters by the Welcome of
# the commit that added it.
instance dilla
client owner
group chat kind=text target=dededededededededededededededede community=none creator=owner
join_many chat 1000
send owner chat everyone is here
expect_decrypts chat-2 chat everyone is here
expect_decrypts chat-500 chat everyone is here
expect_decrypts chat-1001 chat everyone is here
expect_decrypts_all chat-1001
